license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/erenup/segre-secant-cohen-macaulay"
abstract: >-
  For every r >= 5 and all a, b >= 3 with a + b >= r + 2 and c >= r, the
  reduced affine variety of complex tensors of border rank at most r in
  C^a (x) C^b (x) C^c fails Serre's condition S2 and is not
  Cohen-Macaulay. Its dimension is D = r(a+b+c-2) and its homogeneous
  vertex has depth less than D. This includes the rank-five variety in
  format 3x4x5 and the unit-tensor orbit closures in format r x r x r for
  every r >= 5, and disproves the universal arithmetic Cohen-Macaulay
  conjecture for Segre secants. The paper also determines normalization
  fibres, the completed local ring at a rank-five witness and boundary
  models at specified higher-rank witnesses. Includes the paper,
  plain-text proofs, exact supporting checks, and Lean proofs of two
  finite certificate layers. Files outside paper/ are licensed under MIT;
  files in paper/, including the manuscript source and PDF, are licensed
  under CC BY-SA 4.0.
